A no-op change prints an empty stdout and leaves the file byte-identical; the success summary line goes on stderr, not stdout.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
status: ready
title: Probe plan
sp: 0
---

Body paragraph one.
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md status=ready
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: status=ready
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
status: ready
title: Probe plan
sp: 0
---

Body paragraph one.
-- exit --
0
